5th ascension, previous ones were an elven wiz, dwarven valk, chaotic
knight and a chaotic human wizard. Next I'll try with rogues.

Summary: ascended, dragon scales of all the 9 colors for a fashion show in
the Demigods', /oDeath got only one Rodney out of seven, the others I had
to fight hand-to-hand.


Didn't take any notes, but here's what I remember.

Started the game Jul. 13th, ascended Jul. 21st and played the game on two
different machines (started with 3.4.1 on computer #1, continued with 3.4.3
on computer #2, tried to continue with 3.4.1 (#1), but had to upgrade).


A bookshop had many ?oID and 3-4 ?oEW, some of which were blessed. At this
point katana went to +6. Sacfest (played a spellcaster-fighter for a little
while) on one of the many altars gave Snickersnee and
Trollsbane. #twoweaponed Snickersnee with the katana.

A throne (lots of opulent throne rooms, too) gave me +3SDSM. I preferred
SDSM over GDSM, because I wanted to #twoweapon and wanted to keep the
amulet slot free for something else. Good choice, since "oLS I found
mysteriously disappeared in a military barrack. Didn't notice that at the
moment. HPs didn't drop dramatically, so it must have been a /oD before the
SDSM, or a cockatrice.

Did the quest without MR, Asikaga Takauji died of natural causes induced by
/oDeath. One of his comrades took the Tsurugi so I had to /oD him too.

Used Tsurugi for a while, but after another sacfest had
Firebrand. Enchanted Firebrand to +4, and dual wielded with the katana
until Castle.

Castle was quite easy. Well, maybe a confused ?oTaming had something to do
with it, but only really tough monsters were a lich and a jabbervock. There
was also two peaceful ki-rins outside the castle, don't remember ever seen
two of them on the same level. At least not with XP of 14.

/oW(0:3) gave me [oMR, gauntlets of strength, speedboots, helm of telepathy
and the Grayswandir (had already several ?oCharging). Now I was ready.

Asmodeus was on the level below Valley; a pushover who never hit me second
time. He didn't even teleport to heal. The same happened with Juiblex, he
didn't swallow me. Went hand-to-hand on Vlad, no worries. Baalzebub and
Orcus had some more work on them, 'cause they teleported to heal couple of
times.

The VS was on level 49, and I noticed that I only had 3 candels. c?oTele
and =oTC helped me to get to Minetown, where Izchak was happy to sell me 7
candels more. Then to meet Rodney. Got the book, c?oTele to VS-level, bell,
candelabrum, book, downstairs.

Rodney appeared briefly before the actual sanctum but didn't attack
me. When I hit him, he 'ported away (to the temple, I guess?). Temple had
two Rodneys, /oDeath got the another one (the only time /oDeath managed to
hit him) and the highpriest, Grayswandir and katana the another. Took the
"oY, inspected the remainder of the lot (and tinned Rodney) and c!oGL:ed
out of there.

Mysterious force kicked me downwards 3 or 4 times, something around 10
levels altogether.


The first three planes went quite fast, air elementals were the only
consern, but even they managed to take only 100 of the max. Vortices helped
me there, though. The Plane of Water was annoying. Not because of the
drowning attacks, but because the portal didn't want to come to the same
bubble I was in. Well it did once, but on the far end, where I couldn't
reach it in time. Here I tamed some pets (2 dragons, owlbear and
somethingorother) to bring up with me to the Astral.

Amaterasu Omikami gave me his guardian angel (never used conflict). Headed
right to face Famine (IMO the least scary of the bunch). The altar was
chaotic. Could've used [oOA which I had in BoH, didn't. The middle altar
was guarded by Pestilence and was neutral. Since the only death for me on
Astral happened against Death (http://tinyurl.com/59b8v), I wielded
!oParalysis and smacked him on the forehead with it.

Before offering the amulet, I whistled my for my remaining pets; only
the guardian angel was still alive. Forgot to light the Candelabrum, damn.


